From 4aa4f23a9b0e28d56598f2e4df9d6e7a9f0b4c21 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ChatGPT <patches@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 1 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: add hydrogenx governor for pissarro

Add a lightweight third-party cpufreq governor named hydrogenx.  It is
based on the kernel 4.14 dbs governor framework used by ondemand and is
intended for MT6877/pissarro-style Android kernels where fast ramp-up,
slower ramp-down and userspace boost pulses are useful for frame pacing.

The governor exposes tunables under the governor sysfs directory:
sampling_rate, up_threshold, down_threshold, hispeed_load, hispeed_freq,
min_sample_time, powersave_bias, fast_ramp_down, boost_duration_ms,
boostpulse, ignore_nice_load and io_is_busy.

Enable hydrogenx as the default governor in the pissarro defconfigs.
